-- LQA evidence for the Cat Act 2011 (WA) run cat-act-2011-lqa, step 8A, 2026-10-02.
-- Against the Cat Act 2011 compilation 00-l0-01 and the Cat Regulations 2012 compilation
-- 02-b0-00. Each section names the finding (incidents.json) it evidences. Not part of the
-- encoding certified at 6H and not listed in coverage.json: it only calls the certified modules
-- on new facts. Every person, cat and company here is invented. Where a finding rests on a fork,
-- the reading taken (A) and the reading rejected are both asserted.

§ `Fixtures`

`the holidays` MEANS LIST `the date` 2026 12 25, `the date` 2026 12 28, `the date` 2027 1 1, `the date` 2027 1 26

GIVEN n IS A STRING, vet IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person`
`a resident` n `who is a veterinarian` vet MEANS `Person` WITH
    `name`                            IS n
    `date of birth`                   IS `the date` 1980 1 1
    `parents or guardians`            IS EMPTY
    `became resident in the State on` IS JUST (`the date` 2000 1 1)
    `convictions`                     IS EMPTY
    `is a veterinarian`               IS vet
    `is a veterinary nurse`           IS FALSE
    `units of competency completed`   IS EMPTY
    `courses completed`               IS EMPTY
    `is an approved cat breeder`      IS FALSE
    `is an eligible pensioner`        IS FALSE

`Ana` MEANS `a resident` "Ana" `who is a veterinarian` FALSE
`Ben` MEANS `a resident` "Ben" `who is a veterinarian` FALSE
`Dr Vu` MEANS `a resident` "Dr Vu" `who is a veterinarian` TRUE
-- Dr Hart is registered in Victoria and practises only there. The Veterinary Practice Act 2021
-- s 22(1)(c) makes an interstate practitioner a registered "interstate veterinarian" only if the
-- person "practises veterinary medicine in this State", so for the Cat Act she is not a
-- "veterinarian" (s 3(1); REF-14 supplies the status as a fact).
`Dr Hart, Melbourne` MEANS `a resident` "Dr Hart" `who is a veterinarian` FALSE

